over the past two decades motorcycle  world Lake Constance has become the  leading trade fair for motorbikes in  southern Germany Austria and Switzerland  it showcases all the latest products and  trends this year 807 bikes were on show  including 47 new models there were 20  different shows the three days in late  January were a taste of heaven for  bikers the classic journalist andreas  ilk says classic styles continued to be  in this year bikes with a retro look are  all the rage but customized and  reconfigured to fulfill the owners  wishes the BMW r90 is one such bike a  pure authentic design with plenty of  customizing options this Ducati  scrambler embodies the principle of less  is more the design is a mix of the  traditional and the modern the look is a  tribute to the wild 60s while the  technology is cutting-edge  Kawasaki may be renowned for its sporty  modern bikes but it's Vulcan s and  Vulcan vn900 also have a clearly retro  look  andreas points to technical advances  such as cornering abs which lets you  break hard even while leaning into a  bend without losing control that is a  huge advance another safety feature is  the gear shift assistant so far only BMW  has had it but this year other  manufacturers are set to introduce it it  lets you change gear with a simple kick  without using the clutch very practical  in rush-hour traffic this year the best  bike Awards sported the motto tuned and  pimped 24 distinctive customized bikes  were displayed they boasted all kinds of  special features this one is made of  wood and it even works  at the fair there was a special  exhibition on the history of the fabled  NSU brand put on in cooperation with a  German bicycle and NSU museum it showed  legendary motorbikes from the 1960s  including some great racing models  and then there were bikes that just make  you long for summer like this three  seater electoral tricycle byra waka it  is the first electrode trike to boast  100 kilowatts and a range of 120  kilometers  the slingshot by Polaris is a fun trike  for to its top speed is 220 kilometers  an hour and it takes just 5.6 seconds to  go from nought to 100 think how nice it  would be to take it out for a spin on a  warm summer's day  you
 

